<title>SOUTH KOREA: KSE suspends trading in Shindongbang.</title>
<headline>KSE suspends trading in Shindongbang.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Korea Stock Exchange halted trading in Shindongbang's shares on Thursday because the company had misinformed the exchange about its interest in taking a controlling stake in Midopa Department Store, a bourse statement said.</p>
<p>Trading will resume on Saturday, the statement said.  </p>
<p>Shindongbang's shares stood at 43,500 won before trading was halted.</p>
<p>Shindongbang told the exchange on Thursday it was considering a hostile takeover bid to buy Midopa, an important affiliate of the Dainong Group.</p>
<p>But the edible oil company had said in January it had no intention to acquire Midopa.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5647</p>
</text>
